# A4H Times
## Permanent URL: anandsinhausa.com/a4h/times

---

### How this works
One permanent directory. One file. Replaced every month.
The URL never changes. The content does.

---

### First-time setup (do this once)

**Step 1 — Create the directory**
In your hosting file manager or via FTP/SFTP, navigate to `/a4h/` and create a folder named `times`.

Full path on server:
```
/a4h/times/
```

**Step 2 — Rename your file**
Rename `times-issue-00.html` → `index.html`

**Step 3 — Upload**
Upload `index.html` into `/a4h/times/`

Final path on server:
```
/a4h/times/index.html
```

**Step 4 — Verify**
```
https://anandsinhausa.com/a4h/times
```

---

### Every month (Issue 01, 02, 03 ...)

**Step 1 — Archive the current issue (optional but recommended)**
Before overwriting, save a copy of the current `index.html` with the issue number:
```
/a4h/times/archive/issue-00.html
/a4h/times/archive/issue-01.html
```
This preserves past editions at their own URLs without affecting the main page.

**Step 2 — Rename the new file**
Rename the new month's file → `index.html`

**Step 3 — Overwrite**
Upload the new `index.html` into `/a4h/times/`, replacing the previous one.

The URL `anandsinhausa.com/a4h/times` now shows the new issue automatically.

---

### Notes
- No build step. No dependencies. Each index.html is fully self-contained.
- All images are embedded — no separate image folder needed.
- Google Fonts loads from CDN; page still renders if offline.
- If the URL shows `/index.html` instead of resolving cleanly, confirm your host has `DirectoryIndex index.html` set (most do by default).
